\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Far round the world 
\par Thy children sing their song:
\par From East and West 
\par their voices sweetly blend,
\par Praising the Lord 
\par in whom young lives are strong,
\par Jesus our Guide, 
\par our Hero, and our Friend.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Where Thy wide ocean, 
\par wave on rolling wave,
\par Beats through the ages, 
\par on each island shore,
\par They praise their Lord, 
\par whose hand alone can save,
\par Whose sea of love 
\par surrounds themevermore
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thy sun-kissed children 
\par on earth'sspreading plain,
\par Where Asia's rivers 
\par water all the land.
\par Sing, as they watch 
\par Thy fields of glowing grain,
\par Praise to The Lord 
\par who feeds them with His hand.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Still there are lands 
\par where none have seen Thy face,
\par Children whose hearts 
\par have never shared Thy joy;
\par Yet Thou wouldst pour 
\par on these Thy radiant grace.
\par Give Thy glad strength 
\par to every girl and boy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. All round the world 
\par let children sing Thy song:
\par From East and West 
\par their voices sweetly blend,
\par Praising the Lord 
\par in whom young lives are strong,
\par Jesus our Guide, 
\par our Hero, and our Friend. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

